b:["$","$1","c",{"children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","section",null,{"className":"relative overflow-hidden bg-blue-950 py-20 text-white","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-950 via-blue-950/90 to-blue-900/60"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"container relative mx-auto px-6","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-cyan-300","children":"Institution"}],["$","h1",null,{"className":"mt-3 max-w-3xl text-4xl font-bold leading-tight sm:text-5xl","children":"Word from the Director General"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-8 text-blue-100","children":"Training talent. Raising ambitions. Building Africa's future."}]]}]]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"container mx-auto px-6 py-16","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"mx-auto grid max-w-5xl gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[240px_1fr] lg:items-start","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"relative mx-auto overflow-hidden rounded-3xl bg-white shadow-xl lg:sticky lg:top-24","children":[["$","$L12",null,{"src":"/images/documents/dg-seance-travail.jpg","alt":"Sokhna Maryama Thiam, Director General of ABS — African Business School","width":480,"height":600,"className":"h-[320px] w-full object-cover object-top","priority":true}],["$","div",null,{"className":"p-5","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-slate-950","children":"Sokhna Maryama Thiam"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-slate-500","children":"Director General"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1 text-xs text-slate-400","children":"ABS — African Business School"}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[[["$","p","0",{"className":"text-xl font-medium leading-8 text-slate-900","children":"Dear visitors, dear parents, dear students and partners,"}],["$","p","1",{"className":"mt-5 leading-8 text-slate-600 first:mt-0","children":"It is with conviction and determination that I welcome you to the website of ABS — African Business School."}],["$","p","2",{"className":"mt-5 leading-8 text-slate-600 first:mt-0","children":"Our ambition is clear: to contribute to educating a competent, responsible and bold African generation, capable of understanding the changes in the world, of innovating and of taking an active part in the development of our societies."}],["$","p","3",{"className":"mt-5 leading-8 text-slate-600 first:mt-0","children":"I am deeply convinced that a diploma is not an end in itself, but the starting point of a genuine personal and professional journey. Success rests on the solidity of knowledge, the mastery of skills, the richness of experience, the quality of judgement and the strength of human values. It also requires understanding one's environment, anticipating its changes and turning challenges into opportunities for action."}],["$","p","4",{"className":"mt-5 leading-8 text-slate-600 first:mt-0","children":"It is this conception of education that underpins our commitment at ABS. We want to combine academic rigour with professional practice, skill development with personal fulfilment, and knowledge with the capacity to act. Our ambition is to prepare women and men capable of thinking with rigour, undertaking with boldness, deciding with discernment and exercising their responsibilities with integrity."}],["$","p","5",{"className":"mt-5 leading-8 text-slate-600 first:mt-0","children":"In a world profoundly transformed by digital technology and artificial intelligence, mastering technology has become a strategic issue. We intend to prepare our students for these changes, while preserving an essential conviction: technology must remain at the service of human intelligence, dignity and collective progress."}],"$L13","$L14","$L15","$L16","$L17","$L18"],"$L19","$L1a","$L1b","$L1c","$L1d"]}]]}]}],"$L1e"]}],null,"$L1f"]}]
